# 2026-09-26 security hotfix — this file did not exist before, and its
# absence is exactly why the production incident on this date happened:
# the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` copied this directory's entire contents,
# including .env (every provider API key, the admin key), directly into
# the image at build time. A later, unrelated env-var-only fix (deleting
# a compromised key from Railway) then had no effect at runtime, because
# the process fell back to the still-baked-in .env file the moment the
# real environment variable was absent — see project_mistral_key_
# exposure_incident.md (Claude memory) for the full incident this closes.
#
# Every pattern below is either a credential, a local/dev-only database,
# or a build-irrelevant artifact — nothing here should ever need to be
# inside a production image regardless of this specific incident.

# ── Credentials — the actual point of this file ──────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*_credentials.json
*serviceaccount*.json
credentials.json

# ── Local/dev-only databases and their journal files ─────────────────
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db.bak*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ── Local repair/backup artifacts that have shown up as untracked
#    files in this directory during real incidents this engagement —
#    never something a production image should ship. ─────────────────
*repair*.json
ig_dev.db*

# ── Version control / editor / OS noise ───────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# ── Python build/test artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ── Local dependency lockfile artifacts not needed at image-build time
#    (the Dockerfile installs via pip -e . against pyproject.toml only —
#    see that RUN step's own comment) ─────────────────────────────────
.uv-cache/
